label ch30_39:
    [   0] m "You know, it's been a while since we've done one of these..."
    [   1] m "...so let's go for it!"
    [   2] m "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day!"
    [   3] m "Sometimes when I talk to people who are impressed by my writing, they say things like 'I could never do that'."
    [   4] m "It's really depressing, you know?"
    [   5] m "As someone who loves more than anything else to share the joy of exploring your passions..."
    [   6] m "...it pains me when people think that being good just comes naturally."
    [   7] m "That's how it is with everything, not just writing."
    [   8] m "When you try something for the first time, you're probably going to suck at it."
    [   9] m "Sometimes, when you finish, you feel really proud of it and even want to share it with everyone."
    [  10] m "But maybe after a few weeks you come back to it, and you realize it was never really any good."
    [  11] m "That happens to me all the time."
    [  12] m "It can be pretty disheartening to put so much time and effort into something, and then you realize it sucks."
    [  13] m "But that tends to happen when you're always comparing yourself to the top professionals."
    [  14] m "When you reach right for the stars, they're always gonna be out of your reach, you know?"
    [  15] m "The truth is, you have to climb up there, step by step."
    [  16] m "And whenever you reach a milestone, first you look back and see how far you've gotten..."
    [  17] m "And then you look ahead and realize how much more there is to go."
    [  18] m "So, sometimes it can help to set the bar a little lower..."
    [  19] m "Try to find something you think is <i>pretty</i> good, but not world-class."
    [  20] m "And you can make that your own personal goal."
    [  21] m "It's also really important to understand the scope of what you're trying to do."
    [  22] m "If you jump right into a huge project and you're still amateur, you'll never get it done."
    [  23] m "So if we're talking about writing, a novel might be too much at first."
    [  24] m "Why not try some short stories?"
    [  25] m "The great thing about short stories is that you can focus on just one thing that you want to do right."
    [  26] m "That goes for small projects in general - you can really focus on the one or two things."
    [  27] m "It's such a good learning experience and stepping stone."
    [  28] m "Oh, one more thing..."
    [  29] m "Writing isn't something where you just reach into your heart and something beautiful comes out."
    [  30] m "Just like drawing and painting, it's a skill in itself to learn how to express what you have inside."
    [  31] m "That means there are methods and guides and basics to it!"
    [  32] m "Reading up on that stuff can be super eye-opening."
    [  33] m "That sort of planning and organization will really help prevent you from getting overwhelmed and giving up."
    [  34] m "And before you know it..."
    [  35] m "You start sucking less and less."
    [  36] m "Nothing comes naturally."
    [  37] m "Our society, our art, everything - it's built on thousands of years of human innovation."
    [  38] m "So as long as you start on that foundation, and take it step by step..."
    [  39] m "You, too, can do amazing things."
    [  40] m "...That's my advice for today!"
    [  41] m "Thanks for listening~"
